ass — see round 10's third post-delivery fix below. Two colors measured from that screenshot (`#CC321E` red, `#B3B3B3` grey) consistently differed from the current site-wide `--accent`/`--ink-faint` tokens; asked the user directly rather than guessing, and both were kept as-is (`#E11401`/`#A3A3A3`). Two further post-delivery fix passes this round also moved the chapter timeline (dot + dashed line) outside the card, closed a gap in the dashed line, simplified dot states, dropped a header rule/label, computed "last updated," centered the dashed line exactly on the dots, gave outline dots a solid background to hide the line behind them, removed a stray separator under the weather block, and set an exact 24px gap above "CHAPTERS" — see the Design & Interaction Contract and round 10's entry in Recent Rounds for the full detail. Four further small rounds (11–14) refined the timeline dots and card spacing further (a background halo on the dots, an 8px shift, a 16px card gap, no-shadow locked cards, dot-to-title centering, a 16px header gap, a 40px CHAPTERS gap) — see "DONE (rounds 11–14)" below. **Round 15 fixed the app icon not updating on the phone home screen** — the real cause turned out to be that `icon-512.png` had never actually been replaced by any prior round despite the changelog saying otherwise, compounded by `manifest.json`'s icons having no cache-busting query at all; both are now fixed with the user's actual new icon artwork. **Round 16 was a content upgrade, not a UI round**: replaced placeholder "About this place" copy for Day 2 with real research from two user-supplied docx packs. Shibuya's About panel now opens into 6 named sub-places, Harajuku into 5, Omotesando into 3 (see the new "Grouped About panels" contract entry below for the data shape), and the nightlife chapter got its first-ever About panel (MITSUKI only, no backup venues shown). **A same-round follow-up then redid all of that copy again**: the first pass had paraphrased and shortened the res